{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1073773-roleplaying-zeus-or-hades-as-your-totem","id":1073773,"title":"Roleplaying Zeus or Hades as your totem.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-05T09:44:44-07:00","id":1073773,"title":"Roleplaying Zeus or Hades as your totem.","content":"I am trying to think of some good inspiration for having a Greek god as a totem. What would it be like to be a permanent worshipper and what would your responsibilities be like? Also, what abilities might you gain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:09:41-07:00","id":1073783,"title":"","content":"For starters, the original worshipers of Zeus saw the god primarily as a weather deity. They built him altars and monuments on mountaintops as close to the sky as possible. Offerings of wine were made in hopes that Zeus would bring rain in times of drought. An oracle for Zeus interpreted the sounds of wind in the branches of sacred oak trees as messages from Zeus.<br /> <br /> Dedicating tall structures in high places to the Glory of the mighty Zeus and giving offerings of sacrificial animals, cakes, and wine (depending on where in Greece you were) seemed to be the thing to do.<br /> <br /> Zeus was also supposed to be a champion of justice and tradition, particularly the rights of hospitality. These must be a big thing for Zeus worshipers.<br /> (The respect from host to guest. The host must be hospitable to the guest and provide him/her with food, drink, bath and gifts when they leave. It is not polite to ask questions until the guest has finished the meal provided to them. The respect from guest to host. The guest must be courteous to the host and not be a burden. The guest should also provide a gift if they have one)<br /> <br /> Animals sacred to Zeus were the Eagle and the bull. Plants sacred to Zeus were the Holm Oak and Olive tree.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Scion book. Awareness, Command, Integrity, Presence, Politics, &amp; Thrown were under his purview. In Mage these would probably be Alertness, Awareness, Intimidation, Leadership, Politics, &amp; Athletics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T12:03:33-07:00","id":1073818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1073773-roleplaying-zeus-or-hades-as-your-totem?p=1073783#post1073783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For starters, the original worshipers of Zeus saw the god primarily as a weather deity. They built him altars and monuments on mountaintops as close to the sky as possible. Offerings of wine were made in hopes that Zeus would bring rain in times of drought. An oracle for Zeus interpreted the sounds of wind in the branches of sacred oak trees as messages from Zeus.<br /> <br /> Dedicating tall structures in high places to the Glory of the mighty Zeus and giving offerings of sacrificial animals, cakes, and wine (depending on where in Greece you were) seemed to be the thing to do.<br /> <br /> Zeus was also supposed to be a champion of justice and tradition, particularly the rights of hospitality. These must be a big thing for Zeus worshipers.<br /> (The respect from host to guest. The host must be hospitable to the guest and provide him/her with food, drink, bath and gifts when they leave. It is not polite to ask questions until the guest has finished the meal provided to them. The respect from guest to host. The guest must be courteous to the host and not be a burden. The guest should also provide a gift if they have one)<br /> <br /> Animals sacred to Zeus were the Eagle and the bull. Plants sacred to Zeus were the Holm Oak and Olive tree.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Scion book. Awareness, Command, Integrity, Presence, Politics, &amp; Thrown were under his purview. In Mage these would probably be Alertness, Awareness, Intimidation, Leadership, Politics, &amp; Athletics</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, but what about Hades?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T12:36:47-07:00","id":1073828,"title":"","content":"As for Hades, he was honored in burial rites wherein there was mourning and the deceased was given coin so he or she could go to the river Styx and pay the ferryman for passage to the lands of the dead, and in necromantic ceremonies involving communion with the ghosts of the dead. Supposedly, ghosts were attracted by offerings of blood from sacrificed animals or contacted through psychedelic trips to the underworld near (or in) caves (gates to the underworld). Worshipers also pounded the ground with their fists so that Hades could hear their prayers.<br /> <br /> Apparently, black animals (usually sheep) were common sacrifices to Hades and he vehemently rejects human sacrifice. Blood sacrifices were dripped into a pit in the ground as the person making the offering averted their face.<br /> <br /> While stern, unyielding, and without pity, he was still considered to be a champion of Justice.<br /> He was the god of the underworld and also of the wealth that comes from under the Earth.<br /> <br /> Scion has his Abilities as Academics, Command, Occult, Presence, Stealth, Thrown In Mage these would probably be Alertness, Awareness, Intimidation, Leadership, Academics, Occult, Esoterica, &amp; Stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-05-2017, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:56:29-07:00","id":1073867,"title":"","content":"Shape-shifting your way into the pants of as many women as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:52:58-07:00","id":1073913,"title":"","content":"What is your Paradigm and how does your character see them? In the Umbra you could just as readily meet the most Homer of Zeuses or the far more Proper Jupiter or even a Kirby Space God. So is your character of a lost order that's handed things down? a reconstructionist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:53:39-07:00","id":1075701,"title":"","content":"Hollow One, with a blend of Hermetic and Dream Speaker for a paradigm. He wants to be a Necromancer and he wants to be a bridge between the living and dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:57:05-07:00","id":1075704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https