:"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:01:30-07:00","id":1077547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1073773-roleplaying-zeus-or-hades-as-your-totem?p=1075701#post1075701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hollow One, with a blend of Hermetic and Dream Speaker for a paradigm. He wants to be a Necromancer and he wants to be a bridge between the living and dead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So he's generally a reconstructionist. He has to piece together his Gods from the stories he he has and what he thinks makes sense. Rather than going with origional looks I'd try to see how Zeus and Hades might be incorporated into modern things. Entering the underworld via elevator for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:50:51-07:00","id":1078125,"title":"","content":"F-15s as his sacred eagles, delivering thunderbolts in the form of Sidewinder missiles and a Vulcan gatling gun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avat